  (text "J-UMB-INST: the instrument's etherCON, on the umbilical adapter (PCB-UMB-ADAPTER).   J-UMB: the header joining the adapter to the main board.   J-UMB-MOD: the module panel's etherCON.\nPin N of all three is one net: the adapter's tracks and CABLE-UMB (a straight Cat5e lead) are not parts. Which board carries which part: spi-link.md, 'Which board places what'." (at 25.4 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid b78ba3e0-f8c9-5295-8af2-c2713305a7ca))
  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity: THE UMBILICAL ITSELF.\n\nThis circuit is named for the SPI half and it carries all eight conductors. J-UMBILICAL is one connector with one pin\nmap - umbilical-pinmap - and four of its eight belong to other circuits' nets: the breath pair is\ninterfaces/breath-sense-link's and the power pair is the load switch's and the module's star's. They are declared here\nbecause the CONNECTOR is here, not because the nets are.\n\nTHE CABLES ARE NOT COMPONENTS. CABLE-UMB is a straight Cat5e patch lead: pin N to pin N, with no pin map of its own to\nget wrong. Netting sixteen conductor ends to say \"1 goes to 1\" would add length and no truth.\n\nINSIDE THE INSTRUMENT THERE IS NO CABLE (ADR 0021). J-UMB-INST, behind the tail cap, is soldered to the umbilical\nadapter, whose tracks run its pin N to J-UMB pin N, and J-UMB - a right-angle header - is soldered into both the adapter\nand the main board. The adapter's tracks are not components either. So J-UMB, J-UMB-INST and J-UMB-MOD pin N are one net\neach, and J-UMB is where the carrier's nets actually reach the umbilical. It is declared HERE, not in carrier/carrier,\nbecause it is the umbilical's connector with the umbilical's pin map, and splitting the eight nets at it would give\nevery port in this file a second name for the same node.\n\nTHIS CIRCUIT'S OWN THREE BOM ROWS ARE PLACED ELSEWHERE, and that is correct: it derives R-SPI-PULL's values and\nR-SPI-SER's 100 ohm, but the six pulls are on the module board (module/digital-and-supervision) and the three series\nresistors are on the carrier (carrier/carrier). Owning a row and placing an instance are different things.\n\nTHE PAIRING IS THE ARGUMENT, not the numbering. Each signal travels with its own return in a twisted pair: BREATH with\nAGND, +12V with PWR_GND, SCLK with MOSI, CS with DIG_GND.\n\n[DIG_GND] TIED TO THE MAIN BOARD'S GROUND AT J-UMB (ADR 0018). carrier/carrier joins DIG_GND to its PWR_GND at pin 8 through NT-DIG, a net tie: copper, nothing bought. The net keeps its name because at the module end conductor 8 is its own net, and\nwhere it meets AGND_MOD there is dig-gnd-topology (disputed)." (at 25.4 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid efcb62e8-c39f-57cd-9a0e-eeee73982870))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
